hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19231","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi from Abu Hazim al-Tammar from al-Bayadi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the people while they were praying and their voices had risen in recitation. He said: The worshipper converses with his Lord, so let him consider what he converses with Him, and none of you should raise his voice over another with the Quran."
